=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The reported symptom — PC11 on VLAN 20 being "completely isolated" — does not
match the live lab state. All connectivity paths were tested and found fully
operational. PC11 (172.16.20.11/24, connected to switch2.eth5) can reach every
tested destination with 0% packet loss: same-VLAN peers PC9 and PC10, its
default gateway 172.16.20.254 (mswitch0's vlan20 SVI), cross-VLAN host PC5 on
VLAN 10, and cross-VLAN host PC12 on VLAN 30. Reverse-path traffic from PC12
back to PC11 also succeeded, confirming bidirectional forwarding.

At the switch layer, switch2.eth5 (the access port feeding PC11) is in UP state,
correctly assigned as a member of the br_vlan20 Linux bridge, and in forwarding
mode with no STP-blocked state. PC11's MAC address is dynamically learned on
that port. The mswitch0 multilayer switch has a healthy vlan20 SVI
(172.16.20.254/24) with active RX/TX counters. No interface is down, no port is
error-disabled, and no VLAN assignment is wrong anywhere in the path.

The helpdesk ticket is a false premise. There is no network fault; PC11 is fully
connected and reachable. The corrective action is to inform the user that the
device is reachable from the network side and to investigate whether the issue
was transient, already self-resolved, or stemmed from a host-side misconfiguration
(e.g., a local firewall rule or a momentary cable pull) that was not present at
the time of this investigation.
=== END ===
